1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:00,430
Okay.

2
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:02,460
Welcome back to Passive Voice.

3
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:09,020
So a couple of more rules and general usage about passive voice.

4
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:16,710
So in previous in the previous part, we talked about the formation of passive voice and we said that

5
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:25,800
it is formed by the verb be plus the past participle, which is the past form of the verb or the third

6
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,600
column or irregular verbs.

7
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:36,050
However, sometimes you can hear, you can see, and you can use get instead of be.

8
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:45,420
So if you look here, sometimes we use get plus past participle to make passive. So be can be changed

9
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:46,620
by get.

10
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,980
So you can use both of them.

11
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:52,860
Let's look at the couple of examples.

12
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:57,930
The programming will get done as soon as we have the requirements.

13
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:02,070
Or Be careful with the database, please.

14
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,820
It might get broken.

15
00:01:04,810 --> 00:01:11,920
And the last one. If you put your iPhone on charge, the iOS will get updated automatically at night.

16
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:20,680
So you see in all of those sentences we've used get instead of be for passive voice, because this is

17
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:24,580
clearly passive, the programming will get done.

18
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:30,820
So this action kind of goes back and will be performed on this object.

19
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:33,000
So this is clearly passive.

20
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:40,420
However we use get. You can use both of them either be or get. The difference

21
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:46,570
The slight difference between them will be that when we say get, for example, in the second example

22
00:01:46,570 --> 00:01:49,510
here, it might get broken.

23
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:54,790
The word get is the synonym, as you know, to the word become.

24
00:01:54,790 --> 00:02:01,180
So if you say it might be broken, it means it is already broken.

25
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:02,980
So it is broken.

26
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:09,250
So be careful because it may not work properly, it may be already broken.

27
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:17,020
But if you say get broken, it means maybe the speaker is afraid that you're going to do something wrong

28
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:22,030
and the database will become broken, because of your actions.

29
00:02:22,030 --> 00:02:22,240
Yes.

30
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:24,970
So it may become or get broken.

31
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:30,910
So this is a slight difference between be and get for passive voice.

32
00:02:32,230 --> 00:02:33,400
Just remember that.

33
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,630
And we move on.

34
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:40,330
And and there are a couple of general things about passive voice usage.

35
00:02:40,330 --> 00:02:42,460
So two bullet points.

36
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:47,920
The first is - use passive with or without the doer of the action.

37
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:50,860
So the door is somebody who does the action.

38
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:54,610
So it's up to you

39
00:02:54,610 --> 00:03:01,960
yeah, you can speak about the doer, you can mention the doer, or you can be completely without the doer

40
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,010
in this sentence.

41
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:09,700
The example would be The invitation was sent today and you can finish it here.

42
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,740
The invitation was sent today.

43
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:19,780
I don't care who send it, so I'm not mentioning the doer of the action. Or if I still want to include

44
00:03:19,780 --> 00:03:21,850
this person or this thing

45
00:03:21,850 --> 00:03:26,770
I can use this word "by" and introduce the doer of the action.

46
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:30,040
So the invitation was sent by PM.

47
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:42,640
Now why would we actually use passive voice and say who did the action in the end of the sentence

48
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:49,330
if we could have just used the active voice? We could say  PM sent the invitation today.

49
00:03:50,210 --> 00:03:53,450
Okay, well, that is a logical question.

50
00:03:53,540 --> 00:04:01,850
And the answer to it is that and this is the bullet point number two, that usually we use passive when

51
00:04:01,850 --> 00:04:07,910
the doer is either not known or not important or it is obvious.

52
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:14,000
So and the example of very good example The hackers will be arrested.

53
00:04:14,510 --> 00:04:15,410
Full stop.

54
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:22,820
I don't need to say who will arrest the hackers, because this is very obvious.

55
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:27,470
It's common knowledge that only the police can arrest somebody.

56
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:30,830
So I don't need to say who will do it.

57
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:36,380
I don't need the doer of the action here, because it's obvious why would I speak about it?

58
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:43,760
So I could have said The hackers will be arrested by the police, but it's obvious that it's police.

59
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:44,180
Yeah.

60
00:04:44,210 --> 00:04:50,900
So in this case, we just form a passive sentence without the door of the action, or when the doer

61
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:51,830
is not known.

62
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:56,870
For example, His bike was stolen.

63
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:58,760
His bike was stolen.

64
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:02,360
I don't know who stole his bike and he doesn't know.

65
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:05,780
So the doer is not known.

66
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:09,080
So we could say somebody stole his bike

67
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,510
Yes, that's also an option.

68
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:15,380
But we can use passive voice for that as well.

69
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,120
Good.

70
00:05:17,810 --> 00:05:24,710
And some other rules are that we when we use passive with the doer

71
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,220
and here, let's pay attention to this one,

72
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:33,680
the focus is shifted from the doer to the object of the action.

73
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:42,500
So if I still want to mention the doer of the action, but I don't want to make them the focus, the

74
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:48,020
centre point of the sentence, because they are less important. In this 

75
00:05:48,170 --> 00:05:55,850
In this case, I use passive voice and I say, for example, The suspicious link in the email was opened

76
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:57,560
by one of our colleagues.

77
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:06,560
So the focus is more on the suspicious link and the the event that the suspicious link in the email

78
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,580
was opened.

79
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,660
And it's less on our colleague.

80
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:18,230
We don't want to make a very big I like to draw a lot of attention to who did the action but to what

81
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:19,220
actually happened.

82
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:24,970
And passive is commonly used in more formal texts.

83
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:31,430
It means academic papers, scientific research and things like reports.

84
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:37,430
So if you're not an academic kind of person, maybe you don't do research papers.

85
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:46,160
However, if you work in IT or you plan to work in it, you're definitely going to need to write a lot

86
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:53,300
of things, emails, reports to fill out different forms and things like that.

87
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:58,970
And for those situations, you will definitely need a passive voice.

88
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:05,120
For example, this is an example of a reporting sentence.

89
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:09,470
The issue is found in all payment methods on the website.

90
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:14,570
The functionality is being retested on the customer side.

91
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:22,430
So you see how these sentences are very precise, very informative.

92
00:07:22,470 --> 00:07:29,480
Yet we don't speak, we don't say any unnecessary details. It's just precise and up to the point.

93
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,790
This is exactly the reporting style.

94
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:36,530
And as you can see, the passive voice is used there.

95
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:38,820
Good.

96
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:47,940
And to wrap up this lesson, let's do a small exercise together for passive voice.

97
