Jayne was fired by Mr. Smith.

108
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:33,600
Okay.

109
00:08:33,690 --> 00:08:38,669
We start with Mr. Smith, because he is the doer of this action.

110
00:08:40,409 --> 00:08:48,870
And we have the formation of a passive voice here, which is was fired.

111
00:08:49,890 --> 00:08:54,060
Now, remember what we spoke about the formation of passive voice.

112
00:08:55,290 --> 00:09:01,350
The main verb which is fired here is always in

113
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:02,670
in which form?

114
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:06,690
Yes, it's in past participle form.

115
00:09:06,690 --> 00:09:09,390
So it's always going to be past participle.

116
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:12,960
It doesn't show the tense of the sentence.

117
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:15,800
We don't know the tense because we just know it's passive.

118
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:17,940
So that's why it's past participle.

119
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:23,190
However, what shows the tense and remember, what does the job is

120
00:09:23,190 --> 00:09:28,230
the verb be and be here is in the past simple form.

121
00:09:29,010 --> 00:09:30,510
So be past simple

122
00:09:30,510 --> 00:09:31,680
was or were.

123
00:09:32,190 --> 00:09:34,360
So Jane was fired.

124
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:38,670
Now we know that this is a passive sentence in past simple.

125
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:43,560
Now we need to create an active sentence using past simple tense.

126
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:47,940
And that would be very easy for this one.

127
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:51,870
Mr. Smith fired Jane.

128
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:53,810
Good.

