Good.

145
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:02,570
And this is our perfect active voice sentence. Now

146
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:07,880
number four. The reports had been completed by the students.

147
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:10,810
Okay.

148
00:11:10,810 --> 00:11:18,910
So as you know, in active sentence, we have to start with the doer of the action, the doer of the

149
00:11:18,910 --> 00:11:19,690
action

150
00:11:20,110 --> 00:11:27,630
in our case, in sentence number four is the students.

151
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:29,460
The students did something.

152
00:11:29,470 --> 00:11:32,410
What did they do? Or what had they done?

153
00:11:32,770 --> 00:11:36,430
Now let's inspect this sentence, the structure.

154
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,600
What tense is it in?

155
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:44,090
We know that completed is in past participle because it's passive. 

156
00:11:44,210 --> 00:11:48,440
So let's look at this form had been.

157
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,030
What form is it?

158
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:52,430
What tense is it? Had

159
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:59,150
and the third form of the verb - had been. Okay

160
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:02,560
this is past perfect tense.

161
00:12:02,570 --> 00:12:03,880
This is past perfect.

162
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:06,800
So we need to use active

163
00:12:07,190 --> 00:12:15,560
past perfect. And the formation is had and the main verb in the third form or with ending -ed.

164
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:25,010
So we say the students had completed the report.

165
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:27,170
Good.

166
